  "summary": "Blind review of the r2 candidate (persisted at /tmp/aurum-reviews/AUR-360-r2-reviewA.md): APROVADO. RED typed, GREEN stable across two runs (b71d3f62...), container and host agree. Every lock field was re-derived by the reviewer against the real go.mod/go.sum; the field-by-field cross-check was proven non-decorative by three extra vectors (go.mod tamper, go.sum module added without digest update, and go.sum module added WITH digest updated, which still fails go_lock_mismatch through the bijection loop). One non-blocking finding recorded: the card's Public contract enumerates four codes while MUT-001/MUT-002 name two others literally; .board/cards is forbidden_paths for this card, so the author documents the tension instead of hiding it and a future card must reconcile the card text."
